    "relation": "two public contracts of GTBase.distant_paths over a supplied list of vertex sequences. Raw relation: pairwise_distant_seqs d paths, for every two UNEQUAL sequence values of the list the closed d.-1 set_ball (GTBase.balls) around the support (seq_vertices) of one misses the support of the other; equal duplicates are ignored and nothing requires pathhood, uniqueness or nonempty sequences. X26.x26_pairwise_distant_paths is it by conversion; X39 / X116 / X146 also asked for disjoint supports, a redundant conjunct (every seed set lies in its closed ball), equivalent without premises by pairwise_distant_seqsP. Existence: has_k_distant_set_paths d k X Y, some list of exactly k entries, uniq, every entry a seq_set_path X Y (B5) and pairwise_distant_seqs d; X26's wrapper by conversion, X39's and X116's through has_k_distant_set_pathsP. d = 0 and d = 1 both mean disjoint supports; k = 0 always holds; k = 1 is one X-Y path, a one-vertex path when X and Y meet; closed balls never leave a component. Distinct and untouched: X146's A-path existence chain (frozen, guards kept), X113's distant cycles (radius d) and vertex or triangle distance predicates.",
